\f3\fs26 \'93Alex, we have to speak. This brief is very skinny. It relies entirely on eyewitness identification in only one murder to link him with the rest. The forensic evidence, identical stab wounds patterns, is pretty flimsy and the cause of death for Mr Marrin is listed as both trampling and blood loss.\'94 There wasn\'92t too much more evidence in the file that when she had left the brief with the Commissioner, only a few extra pages of intell and one statement.\
\'93So?\'94\
\'93
\f4\i Novus actus intervenens?
\f3\i0 \'94\
\'93Yes, of course.\'94 Shakti pretended to know.\
\'93You have no idea what I am talking about, do you Alex?\'94\
\'93Not one bit.\'94\
\'93Don\'92t worry about it, that defence probably won\'92t fly, but if he has a decent alibi for the Marrin murder, everything falls to pieces. There is only suspicion attached to the disappearance of Andrea Novetine, but no evidence. His credit card records show he was at the very same places the victims were last seen, but that does not mean murder.\'94 \
\'93It\'92s easier on T.V.\'94 Shakti wished he had just put in a couple of cameras in Cracker\'92s house and then dubbed in a confession.\
\'93Well this is an actual criminal justice matter and to me, evidence counts. If you want to get someone to beat a confession out of him, now is the time to find them.\'94 Hayley waited, but Shakti remained silent. \'93I suggest we start with the most recent murder, James Marrin and the possible connection with the disappearance of Ms Novetine. When we have questioned him for a few hours he will make a mistake. Once that happens he should crack and we can zero in on the other murders. We might be lucky enough to get confessions.\'94\
\'93No beatings at all?\'94 \
\'93Not my style, Lieutenant.\'94 Like all of her colleagues, she had, on occasion roughed up a few crooks during an arrest, but when it came to interviewing she was completely by the book. \'93Even if it does fast track confessions, resorting to violence is the hallmark of a poorly trained and poorly prepared investigator.\'94\
They entered the interview room and saw Cracker, black hood moving back and forth as he sucked in air, seated and handcuffed to a non-descript desk in the centre of the brightly lit room. Shakti ripped off the hood.\
\'93In the name of The Dawkins, what is this all about Alex?\'94 As per procedure, Cracker had not been told why he had been arrested and was feeling very uneasy. \
\'93You are the Nightclub Vampire. We have the evidence. It\'92s all here. Admit it and we will go easy on you. Admit it.\'94 Shakti tried to be professional.\
\'93Lieutenant? Perhaps I may speak to Mr Hardy.\'94 Hayley had to concentrate hard not to roll her eyes, shake her head or punch him in the face. 
\f4\i This is amateur hour.
\f3\i0 \
\'93Okay.\'94\
\'93Mr Hardy. As you are aware, my name is Detective Superintendent Lanning and this is Lieutenant Shakti. We are investigating the death of James Marrin and the disappearance of Andrea Novetine. Shortly I propose to interview you. My questions and any answers you give to those questions will be recorded on both audio and holograph as the interview takes place. Do you understand that?\'94\
\'93Okay. Which interview technique are we using today? Cognitive, Reid or P.E.A.C.E?\'94 Cracker desperately hoped that this might distract her from finishing off her little pre-interview spiel, during which time he hoped he could talk his way out of this. 
\f4\i I hope it is Reid, that is the worst method by far.
\f3\i0 \
\'93What do you know of interview techniques, L.2?\'94 She knew he was trying to distract her, but sometimes, most times, when you let them yap, they trip themselves up. Suspects are convinced they are smarter than any dumb-ass cop and try to establish dominance by ceasing control of the interview. To accomplish this they have to talk and getting a suspect to talk was the battle half won. He could have the illusion of dominance, but she would have control.\
\'93I have been required, recently, to brain-dump all of the police regulations and procedures. I have been helping a friend out.\'94 Cracker stared directly at Shakti and shook his head. \'93Look, I don\'92t even know James Minion. When am I supposed to have killed him?\'94\
\'93James Marrin. Between 10.00pm on 21 February and 12.30am on 22 March this year.\'94 Hayley had every detail of this brief memorised and categorized. \
\'93That does not ring a bell.\'94\
\'93Let me refresh your memory. It was the night of the Stick it Inn bombing. He was found stabbed and trampled to death in the street after the crowds had been cleared.\'94\
\'93I have two people who can account for my whereabouts on the night. I assisted a woman by the name of Sarah Jacobson out of the bombed nightclub and then later we both went to help Lieutenant Shakti clean up the public hygiene facility. Isn\'92t that right Shakti?\'94 The Lieutenant was looking for a place to hide, but no hole appeared in the floor to mercifully swallow him up.\
\'93Oh, Come on! You know him, Shakti? You knew he was with you when Marrin was killed? You cannot be fucking serious.\'94 Detective Lanning was beside herself.\
\'93I didn\'92t look at the dates.\'94\
\'93I am exasperated beyond belief, Alex. Did you even read the file?\'94\
\'93I tried, it was too long and complicated. All those statements and reports looked pretty impressive and the Commissioner told me to arrest him.\'94\
\'93I am very glad none of this has been recorded. An alibi witness interviewing the suspect! Our illustrious co-workers would have pinned it up on the link for all to see. It\'92s going to be embarrassing enough to explain, but that will be your problem, Alex. You will have to drag this eyewitness in and check out his story. If Mr Hardy was with you and Sarah, then the witness must be lying.\'94 \
Hayley stood up and opened the door and poked her head out into the main office and said to Sarah, \'93How did you go with the disc?\'94\
\'93No-one here knows what it is, but I know someone who might be able to help us. I want official authority to brief him.\'94 Sarah did not want to be accused of leaking information.\
\'93That should not be a problem, but I need you in here for a minute, Sarah. Make sure you bring the disc with you.\'94 
\f4\i It may come in handy.
\f3\i0 \
As Sarah entered the room, the surveillance directly linked to the Commissioner\'92s Office was interrupted. He jumped up and bashed the emitter, but there was nothing by white noise. He had heard more than enough. Picking Shakti for this job was a major mistake, but he reflected, picking him for any job was an act of sheer stupidity. He knew Shakti would fuck up the interview, but it did not matter, once Hardy was placed into processing his fate was certain.\
\'93Shakti, go and chase up that eyewitness and record Anthony Hardy as a suspect in custody, but not charged. Okay?\'94 Hayley was happy for any excuse to get rid of him.\
\'93Yes.\'94 Shakti hoped he would remember.\
\'93Now, you two are going to tell me everything.\'94 Detective Lanning sat down and commenced the interrogation. 
